509
00:31:23,460 --> 00:31:25,360
The vibrant colors have more purpose

510
00:31:25,460 --> 00:31:31,300
than aesthetic appeal, but also speak a universal language.

511
00:31:31,400 --> 00:31:33,940
It's designed so it can be used by any kid anywhere

512
00:31:34,040 --> 00:31:35,120
in the world.

513
00:31:35,220 --> 00:31:38,680
The color coding is important because we don't want words.

514
00:31:38,780 --> 00:31:41,180
So just color-coded building instructions

515
00:31:41,280 --> 00:31:44,180
let's see instruction books be clear to everybody.

516
00:31:44,280 --> 00:31:45,980
And that global reach has helped

517
00:31:45,981 --> 00:31:49,580
the toy construction set business into a $20 billion

518
00:31:49,680 --> 00:31:52,480
a year industry.

519
00:31:52,580 --> 00:31:55,380
However, this booming growth has greatly influenced

520
00:31:55,480 --> 00:31:58,720
the manufacturing community.

521
00:31:58,820 --> 00:32:02,220
Toys used to be made just about 100% here.

522
00:32:02,320 --> 00:32:04,140
And over the last 25 years, you've

523
00:32:04,240 --> 00:32:08,140
seen America shed about 45% of their manufacturing jobs

524
00:32:08,240 --> 00:32:10,140
overseas.

525
00:32:10,240 --> 00:32:12,780
But with 95% of its production happening

526
00:32:12,781 --> 00:32:15,580
in the United States,

527
00:32:15,680 --> 00:32:19,020
K'nex is creating more jobs for U.S. workers.

528
00:32:19,120 --> 00:32:21,520
If we had just designed here

529
00:32:21,620 --> 00:32:23,720
and did everything in China,

530
00:32:23,820 --> 00:32:26,720
then we'd probably have only about 10 or 12 employees here

531
00:32:26,820 --> 00:32:28,420
instead of 200.

532
00:32:28,520 --> 00:32:31,440
And that ripple effect is about another 3,000 jobs

533
00:32:31,540 --> 00:32:33,340
in this area.

534
00:32:33,440 --> 00:32:35,940
According to the U.S. Chamber of Commerce,

535
00:32:36,040 --> 00:32:38,080
for every one manufacturing job,

536
00:32:38,180 --> 00:32:41,080
several more are created in sectors such as supply,

537
00:32:41,081 --> 00:32:43,580
transportation, and web design.

538
00:32:43,680 --> 00:32:46,320
We're able to have Americans helping Americans,

539
00:32:46,420 --> 00:32:49,580
making American toys, kids having fun,

540
00:32:49,680 --> 00:32:50,820
and parents having jobs.

541
00:32:53,320 --> 00:32:55,620
However simple or complex they are,

542
00:32:55,720 --> 00:32:58,740
these miniature playthings will inspire the next generation

543
00:32:58,840 --> 00:33:03,940
of American inventors, builders, and craftsmen.

544
00:33:04,040 --> 00:33:06,240
When you can make things, you can do anything.

545
00:33:06,340 --> 00:33:10,080
And manufacturing things that people love in the United States

546
00:33:10,081 --> 00:33:12,720
says to me that there's quality, there's innovation,

547
00:33:12,820 --> 00:33:14,020
and there's opportunity.

548
00:33:14,120 --> 00:33:16,220
And it's that kind of destiny that America should always

549
00:33:16,320 --> 00:33:17,120
be striving for.

550
00:33:20,920 --> 00:33:24,620
Following the road to all things made in America,

551
00:33:24,720 --> 00:33:27,440
you can't help passing a few banners along the way.

552
00:33:30,300 --> 00:33:32,840
The official flag of the United States

553
00:33:32,940 --> 00:33:35,240
has become one of the most recognizable symbols

554
00:33:35,340 --> 00:33:36,040
in the world.

555
00:33:36,041 --> 00:33:40,440
world. Take a look around.

556
00:33:40,441 --> 00:33:44,880
It's everywhere, adorning public buildings, doorsteps, and lining

557
00:33:44,881 --> 00:33:49,080
neighborhood streets. The American flag is one product

558
00:33:49,081 --> 00:33:53,500
that demands to be made by domestic hands.

559
00:33:53,501 --> 00:33:57,300
Annan Flag Makers in South Boston, Virginia, is one of the

560
00:33:57,301 --> 00:34:00,300
oldest and largest flag manufacturers in the world.

561
00:34:00,301 --> 00:34:09,640
I ship probably pretty close to 18,000 to 20,000 flags a week,

562
00:34:09,641 --> 00:34:14,080
but I ship U.S. flags, I ship foreign country flags,

563
00:34:14,081 --> 00:34:15,980
I ship a lot of custom flags.

564
00:34:15,981 --> 00:34:18,620
We produce more U.S. than we do anything else.

565
00:34:21,620 --> 00:34:24,460
The U.S. flag-making business has come a long way

566
00:34:24,461 --> 00:34:26,960
since the days of Betsy Ross and Mary Pickersgill.

567
00:34:26,961 --> 00:34:33,240
Both considered pioneers in the art of flag making in the late 17 and early 1800s.

568
00:34:34,240 --> 00:34:38,600
Back then it would take a month to make one 30 by 40 foot flag.

569
00:34:42,080 --> 00:34:45,700
Today, that same flag could be made in just a few hours.

570
00:34:47,920 --> 00:34:54,360
The process begins with the arrival of the raw material, or gray goods, which are rolls

571
00:34:54,361 --> 00:34:55,780
of nylon and polyester.

572
00:34:56,960 --> 00:35:00,560
The material needs to first go through the dyeing process

573
00:35:00,660 --> 00:35:05,200
to convert the dull fabric into the flag's signature colors.

574
00:35:05,300 --> 00:35:07,200
We call these jig dyers.

575
00:35:07,300 --> 00:35:10,200
And once we put the material into the dyer,

576
00:35:10,300 --> 00:35:12,780
then it runs back and forth on rollers the whole length.

577
00:35:12,880 --> 00:35:14,740
There's a 3,000-yard roll in there,

578
00:35:14,840 --> 00:35:16,840
and it's running back and forth, running through the dye

579
00:35:16,940 --> 00:35:18,320
at the bottom of the machine.

580
00:35:18,420 --> 00:35:20,620
From the time we put it in to the time we take it out,

581
00:35:20,720 --> 00:35:25,760
it takes us about 10 hours to dye one 3,000-yard roll.

582
00:35:25,761 --> 00:35:31,760
In 1777, the Second Continental Congress passed the First Flag

583
00:35:31,860 --> 00:35:35,760
Act that ordered the flag to hold stripes of red and white

584
00:35:35,860 --> 00:35:39,300
and the base of the star field to be blue.

585
00:35:39,400 --> 00:35:45,820
These three colors symbolize courage, purity, and justice.

586
00:35:45,920 --> 00:35:49,720
Once the dye process is completed, the rolls are to be

587
00:35:49,820 --> 00:35:53,460
cut into cakes, which will allow the three colors to be sewn

588
00:35:53,560 --> 00:35:55,760
together.

589
00:35:55,761 --> 00:35:58,760
These are all automatic sewing machines.

590
00:35:58,860 --> 00:36:00,760
When they load the stripes on,

591
00:36:00,860 --> 00:36:02,760
then the machines will sit there and sew

592
00:36:02,860 --> 00:36:05,760
without an operator actually running the machine.

593
00:36:05,860 --> 00:36:08,760
When the bobbin runs out, they have to put a new bobbin thread in.

594
00:36:08,860 --> 00:36:11,760
If they break a thread, they have to keep up with that.

595
00:36:11,860 --> 00:36:15,760
And one operator usually runs about four machines.

596
00:36:15,860 --> 00:36:18,760
After leaving the automatics department,

597
00:36:18,860 --> 00:36:23,760
the sewn stripes are cut into shorts or longs.

598
00:36:23,761 --> 00:36:27,260
The shorts are attached next to the embroidered starfield,

599
00:36:27,360 --> 00:36:29,060
and the longs go underneath.

600
00:36:33,300 --> 00:36:37,000
The fly hem is then added to prevent the flag from unraveling

601
00:36:37,100 --> 00:36:39,100
and shredding in the wind.

602
00:36:39,200 --> 00:36:42,520
A golden yellow fringe is added to those intended

603
00:36:42,620 --> 00:36:43,720
for interior settings.

604
00:36:47,220 --> 00:36:48,720
The canvas heading is attached.

605
00:36:53,760 --> 00:37:00,760
The brass grommets are inserted, and the flag is folded and boxed

606
00:37:00,761 --> 00:37:01,760
for shipment.

607
00:37:06,760 --> 00:37:10,760
Annan has a rich background in providing flags to some of the

608
00:37:10,761 --> 00:37:13,760
most profound moments in United States history.

609
00:37:13,761 --> 00:37:17,760
We've been making flags for better than 165 years.

610
00:37:17,761 --> 00:37:21,760
We made the flag that was hoisted over Iwo Jima.

611
00:37:21,761 --> 00:37:27,760
We made the flag that was on Abraham Lincoln's coffin.

612
00:37:27,761 --> 00:37:30,760
We made the flag that was posted on the moon.

613
00:37:33,400 --> 00:37:38,520
Since Zachary Taylor took the presidential oath in 1849,

614
00:37:38,521 --> 00:37:43,020
Annan and Company has provided U.S. flags for every inauguration

615
00:37:43,021 --> 00:37:46,760
over the last 160 years.

616
00:37:46,761 --> 00:37:51,760
Well, we make American flags all the way from 4x6 to 5x6

617
00:37:51,761 --> 00:37:55,600
that people wave on a stick all the way up through 30 foot

618
00:37:55,700 --> 00:37:57,500
by 60 foot.

619
00:37:57,600 --> 00:38:00,160
The proportions of the flag were not officially

620
00:38:00,260 --> 00:38:03,600
standardized until President William H. Taft signed the

621
00:38:03,700 --> 00:38:06,400
Executive Order of 1912.

622
00:38:06,500 --> 00:38:11,520
It prescribed the hoist and fly of every flag purchased for the

623
00:38:11,620 --> 00:38:16,320
government shall be a ratio of 10 to 19.

624
00:38:16,420 --> 00:38:19,760
Each year, this facility ships up to a large

625
00:38:19,761 --> 00:38:24,400
Each year, this facility ships out over 500,000 flags

626
00:38:24,500 --> 00:38:26,500
to vendors all over the country.

627
00:38:26,600 --> 00:38:28,600
Along with the stars and stripes,

628
00:38:28,700 --> 00:38:31,700
Annan manufactures every state flag in the Union

629
00:38:31,800 --> 00:38:34,600
and every country flag in the United Nations.

630
00:38:34,700 --> 00:38:38,720
However, not all Annan flags are stitched and embroidered.

631
00:38:38,820 --> 00:38:40,720
Some are printed.

632
00:38:40,820 --> 00:38:43,820
Today, Annan is screen printing what many consider

633
00:38:43,920 --> 00:38:49,760
to be its crowning achievement, the POW MIA flag.

634
00:38:49,761 --> 00:38:52,260
During the height of the Vietnam War,

635
00:38:52,360 --> 00:38:55,160
Annen flag makers was commissioned to create a flag

636
00:38:55,260 --> 00:39:00,000
that honored prisoners of war and those missing in action.

637
00:39:00,100 --> 00:39:04,600
In 1971, the black and white motif was unveiled

638
00:39:04,700 --> 00:39:08,520
and has since become the iconic image for those who have not yet

639
00:39:08,620 --> 00:39:11,420
come home from war.

640
00:39:11,520 --> 00:39:15,920
To this day, it is the only flag ever flown over the White House

641
00:39:16,020 --> 00:39:19,760
alongside the stars and stripes.

642
00:39:19,761 --> 00:39:23,760
The process begins with a scoured fabric that is adhered

643
00:39:23,860 --> 00:39:25,760
to a belt and fed through the line.

644
00:39:29,000 --> 00:39:32,400
The printer will then dispense the liquid dye onto the inkwell

645
00:39:32,500 --> 00:39:35,100
of the screen.

646
00:39:35,200 --> 00:39:38,980
The platform will then drop, allowing for a magnet underneath

647
00:39:39,080 --> 00:39:44,660
the belt to propel a stainless steel rod across the screen,

648
00:39:44,760 --> 00:39:47,160
forcing the liquid dye through its pores.

649
00:39:49,760 --> 00:39:53,100
This process is repeated until the color is completely

650
00:39:53,200 --> 00:39:56,600
deposited into the fabric.

651
00:39:56,700 --> 00:39:58,940
Once the flags are printed, they will

652
00:39:59,040 --> 00:40:04,000
advance to the end of the belt, where the wet ink is dry.

653
00:40:04,100 --> 00:40:07,620
The material travels to the three-bowl washer

654
00:40:07,720 --> 00:40:12,220
to eliminate any excess or residual ink.

655
00:40:12,320 --> 00:40:15,020
Then it's straightened and dried.

656
00:40:19,760 --> 00:40:27,700
From there, the flags are rolled, cut, and ready to be shipped out to vendors across

657
00:40:27,701 --> 00:40:32,380
the country.

658
00:40:32,381 --> 00:40:37,880
With a large number of flags made under one roof, it's no wonder that Annan is one of

659
00:40:37,881 --> 00:40:44,300
the largest flag manufacturers in the world, and all of it made right here in the United

660
00:40:44,301 --> 00:40:45,300
States.

661
00:40:45,301 --> 00:40:49,300
and it prides itself on all of its product being US-made.

662
00:40:49,400 --> 00:40:52,500
We advertise all of our product as US-made.

663
00:40:52,600 --> 00:40:54,640
By rights, it should be made in the USA.

664
00:40:58,240 --> 00:41:02,460
Today, being made in America invokes a new sense of pride

665
00:41:02,560 --> 00:41:07,060
for this country, a collaboration of man and machine

666
00:41:07,160 --> 00:41:10,860
that continues to push American innovation forward,

667
00:41:10,960 --> 00:41:14,460
led by an assembly line of fabricators

668
00:41:14,461 --> 00:41:21,460
engineers, and artists who are filling the shelves

669
00:41:21,560 --> 00:41:25,400
with an array of homegrown products,

670
00:41:25,500 --> 00:41:30,500
carrying on the manufacturing legacy that is made in the USA.

